@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-06-09

Feature: Content-Addressed Blob Keys
  "Hashes content with SHA-256 and maps blob keys to fan-out storage paths under objects/."

  Provides:
    - domain.BlobHashPrefix @source("symbol:BlobHashPrefix")
    - domain.HashReader @source("symbol:HashReader")
    - domain.HashBytes @source("symbol:HashBytes")
    - domain.BlobHex @source("symbol:BlobHex")
    - domain.BlobPath @source("symbol:BlobPath")

  Invariants:
    - Blob keys MUST use the sha256: prefix followed by 64 lowercase hex digits
    - BlobPath MUST return objects/{hash[0:2]}/{hash[2:4]}/{hash} with no file extension

  Scenario (happy-path): Hash a stream
    Given readable content
    When HashReader runs
    Then it returns sha256:<hex> without loading the entire payload into memory first

  Scenario (happy-path): Storage path from key
    Given a valid blob key
    When BlobPath runs
    Then it returns the two-level fan-out path under objects/

  Scenario (negative): Invalid blob key
    Given a string without the sha256: prefix or with bad hex
    When BlobHex or BlobPath runs
    Then it returns a validation error
